DISCREPANCY, resolved: the account was created with -PasswordNeverExpires $true and
-UserPrincipalName "svc-entraconnect@raytakosharkygmail.onmicrosoft.com" specified in the
New-ADUser command handed to Raymond, but this capture shows PasswordNeverExpires: False and
an empty UserPrincipalName. Raymond, asked directly: "modified it, my doing" - a deliberate
edit to the command as given, not a capture error or an accident. Worth noting: leaving
PasswordNeverExpires at its default (False) is arguably the more defensible choice given this
project's own permission-sprawl thesis - a password that never expires on a standing service
account is exactly the kind of "nobody ever revisits it" pattern the thesis is about, even
though it's also Microsoft's own stated recommendation for sync accounts (see report's earlier
note on that tension). Whether the empty UPN matters depends on what the AD DS connector
account actually needs to authenticate - being tracked as an open question until the wizard
step tests it.
